---
description: Project context and planning conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `CLAUDE.md` at the repository root for project context, constraints and
local verification commands.

Planning uses PRDs (`docs/prd/`) for product requirements and ADRs (`docs/adr/`)
for architecture decisions. Reference requirement IDs (e.g. `PROG-03`) and ADR
numbers in commits and PRs. Add an ADR for significant technical decisions; never
rewrite an accepted ADR — supersede it.
